abstract: >-
  Recovered research notes and selected computational audits for Erdős Problem #64,
  including an externally unverified Carr-based theorem candidate asserting that a
  hypothetical minimum-order counterexample satisfies |V_3| >= 2|V_{>=4}| + 3.
keywords:
  - graph theory
  - Erdős–Gyárfás conjecture
  - cycles
  - minimum degree
  - computational audit
  - AI-assisted mathematics
